on/math-academy-id "q-158526" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-5{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-3{x}_{2}^{2}\\le 2{x}_{2}^{2},\\,-5{x}_{3}^{2}\\le 2{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=2(1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 2.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $2.$ But before we conclude that $2$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=2.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(1)^{2}-3(0)^{2}-5(0)^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-158526/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8666dd9-b763-589d-8ae3-af203068f1a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158526"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158468/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "a270ff22-7d68-5ff8-86c3-a7a665ad39f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158468/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "cdb3965e-6e1a-59b7-bdb5-c272462a48b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158468/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "08e8ae0f-8a3f-5049-9f38-4faa202a719d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158468/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "31f3fa42-a72f-54f3-b5ce-d3f63aabddf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158468/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "98e6052c-b92f-532b-9242-b5367a877201" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158468/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a3bf9b0-e466-575e-89f1-8fa1dcdf6adf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158468/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-158468/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" "q-158468/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-158468/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-158468/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-158468/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158468" :question/id #uuid "d5fd20d1-98db-517c-aace-d5d1d5f811ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-158468" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=5{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n5{x}_{1}^{2}\\le 8{x}_{1}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =5{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 8{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =8({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=8(1)=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 8.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $8.$ But before we conclude that $8$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=8.$\n\nNotice that when  $x={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =5{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =5(0)^{2}+8(1)^{2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-158468/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8666dd9-b763-589d-8ae3-af203068f1a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158468"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158528/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "fdf8022b-2437-5927-9c56-bda2b1b38f1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158528/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "68f0d4a5-20a9-5e68-b2fc-6e79f1849d0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158528/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "e4739964-bb68-5cce-b6d0-e5eb2cc92c02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158528/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "717ababa-dfa9-5609-b82a-07dea2dec911" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158528/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "cbd12d9b-14dc-53a2-bfd9-8e515a357d50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158528/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b9d7608-1263-586d-a287-b81d95e22506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158528/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-158528/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-158528/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-158528/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-158528/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-158528/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158528" :question/id #uuid "57626bf6-6fb8-577b-860a-222c6da3f8a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-158528" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-7{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}^{2}\\le 4{x}_{1}^{2},\\,-7{x}_{2}^{2}\\le 4{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-7{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 4{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=4(1)=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 4.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $4.$ But before we conclude that $4$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=4.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-7{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(0)^{2}-7(0)^{2}+4(1)^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-158528/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8666dd9-b763-589d-8ae3-af203068f1a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158528"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138023/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "17164810-98d4-5619-9cb1-63918896c640" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138023/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "910c15ce-4050-59b0-8bfe-c153c3e9f55a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138023/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6aeb03d3-128e-5b82-b5a2-274e33c406c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138023/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "c80e609b-891c-539c-a126-4812f5c666ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138023/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "7171401c-7e56-522d-9f55-d66d06fb6ee9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138023/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8847a1c5-2d26-535d-bd3d-b2707a0c54d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-138023/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-138023/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-138023/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-138023/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-138023/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-138023/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138023" :question/id #uuid "78039968-7f65-5b7c-bc19-419760690ea5" :question/math-academy-id "q-138023" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-3{x}_{3}^{2}\\le 2{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=2(1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 2.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $2.$ But before we conclude that $2$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=2.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(0)^{2}+2(1)^{2}-3(0)^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-138023/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8666dd9-b763-589d-8ae3-af203068f1a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138023"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138018/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "50307521-32b9-5e89-ab20-d9b7f80322e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138018/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "11ea8